**Approach**

Both compute each subproblem once. Memoisation is top-down — recurse and cache — while tabulation is bottom-up, filling a table in dependency order. The program runs both on the same recurrence and counts how many subproblems each actually computes.

**Logic**

The difference that matters in practice: memoisation only computes subproblems *reachable* from the query, while tabulation computes every cell in the table whether or not it is needed. For a sparse state space that is a large saving; for a dense one tabulation wins on constant factors.

Tabulation has no recursion, so no stack-depth risk, and its fixed iteration order makes space optimisation obvious — you can usually keep one or two rows instead of the whole table.

**Program**

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution
{
    private static int _memoComputed, _tableComputed;

    // Top-down: only the states actually reachable from the query.
    private static long Memo(int n, int step, Dictionary<int, long> cache)
    {
        if (n == 0) return 1;
        if (n < 0) return 0;
        if (cache.TryGetValue(n, out long cached)) return cached;

        _memoComputed++;
        return cache[n] = Memo(n - step, step, cache) + Memo(n - (step + 1), step, cache);
    }

    // Bottom-up: every cell, needed or not.
    private static long Table(int n, int step)
    {
        var ways = new long[n + 1];
        ways[0] = 1;

        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++)
        {
            _tableComputed++;
            if (i - step >= 0) ways[i] += ways[i - step];
            if (i - (step + 1) >= 0) ways[i] += ways[i - (step + 1)];
        }

        return ways[n];
    }

    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"{"n",6}{"step",6}{"memo states",14}{"table cells",14}{"agree",8}");

        foreach (var (n, step) in new[] { (20, 1), (40, 5), (100, 10), (100, 25) })
        {
            _memoComputed = _tableComputed = 0;

            long memo = Memo(n, step, new Dictionary<int, long>());
            long table = Table(n, step);

            Console.WriteLine($"{n,6}{step,6}{_memoComputed,14}{_tableComputed,14}{memo == table,8}");
        }

        Console.WriteLine();
        Console.WriteLine("memoisation: only reachable states, follows the recurrence, stack depth");
        Console.WriteLine("tabulation:  every cell, no recursion, easy to reduce to one row");
    }
}
```

